Un-serialise the generator weight pull.

songhappy/torchtitan's `rl` branch wraps the TorchStore pull in a staggered
loop over generator nodes. Because the barrier group spans every generator
rank, the mesh pays `_num_gen_nodes` sequential full-model fetches instead of
one. Measured on Sunspot: 13.0 s per pull at 8 nodes (4 generator nodes)
against 1.63 s at 2 nodes (1 generator node) -- a 4x factor that tracks the
generator node count exactly.

Upstream (pytorch/torchtitan nightly be9c85fb2) has no loop here at all, so
this moves the fork toward upstream rather than away from it.

Applies to: songhappy/torchtitan @ a55da6b4 (branch `rl`).
Verified with `git apply --check` against that revision.

